It can be worked around in a script:
```gdscript
func get_collected_items(item_mask: int) -> int:
	var i: int = completed_sequences - ((completed_sequences >> 1) & 0x55555555);
	i = (i & 0x33333333) + ((i >> 2) & 0x33333333);
	i = (i + (i >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F;
	i *= 0x01010101;
	return  i >> 24;
```
*[Found on Stackoverflow](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/109023/count-the-number-of-set-bits-in-a-32-bit-integer)*
but based on the fact that Godot uses bitmasks quite extensively itself and this is a standard function that helps in dealing with bitmasks, I would argue it is fair to make it a proper Feature.
